<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <article id="privacy-page" class="lbm-about">
    <header class="lbm-hero lbm-about-hero">
      <p class="lbm-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="lbm-hero-title">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lbm-hero-lede">
        The short version: this site collects only what you choose to send, uses it only to reply to
        you, and never sells or shares it. Page views are counted on this site's own server, with no
        cookies and nothing that identifies you. There are no third-party analytics, ads, or trackers.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section
      id="privacy-collect"
      class="lbm-about-section"
      aria-labelledby="privacy-collect-heading"
    >
      <h2 id="privacy-collect-heading">What's collected</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Tutoring inquiries.</strong>
        When you send the form on the <.link navigate={~p"/tutoring"}>Tutoring</.link>
        page, your name, email address, the offering you picked,
        and your message are saved so I can
        reply. Only I can see them.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Work inquiries.</strong>
        The form on the <.link navigate={~p"/work-with-me"}>Work with me</.link>
        page saves your name, email address, organization (if you give one),
        and message, for the same
        reason and with the same access.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Topic suggestions.</strong>
        The Suggest a topic form saves only the text of your suggestion. It doesn't ask for your name
        or email.
      </p>
      <p id="privacy-page-views">
        <strong>Page views.</strong>
        When you open a page, the site adds one to that page's count for the day, along with the
        name of the website that linked you here, if any (for example, news.ycombinator.com). That's
        all it keeps: totals per page per day, with no cookies, no IDs, and nothing tying a view to
        you. If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, your views aren't counted
        at all.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>IP addresses.</strong>
        The forms and page view counting briefly check your IP address to stop spam (a limit on how
        much can be sent in a few minutes). It's held in memory for a short time and never saved.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      id="privacy-cookies"
      class="lbm-about-section"
      aria-labelledby="privacy-cookies-heading"
    >
      <h2 id="privacy-cookies-heading">Cookies and storage</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets one cookie, which the forms need to work securely. It doesn't track you across
        sites. If you pick a light or dark theme, that choice is saved in your own browser and never
        sent anywhere.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="privacy-dont" class="lbm-about-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-dont-heading">
      <h2 id="privacy-dont-heading">What isn't done</h2>
      <p>
        No third-party analytics, no advertising, no tracking pixels, and no selling or sharing of
        your information. Your email address is used only to reply to your inquiry.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="privacy-keep" class="lbm-about-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-keep-heading">
      <h2 id="privacy-keep-heading">Keeping and deleting</h2>
      <p>
        Inquiries are kept only as long as they're useful for replying. You can ask
        for yours to be deleted at any time by emailing <a
          href={"mailto:#{@contact_email}"}
          id="privacy-contact"
        >{@contact_email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're under 13, please have a parent or guardian send the inquiry for you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      id="privacy-hosting"
      class="lbm-about-section"
      aria-labelledby="privacy-hosting-heading"
    >
      <h2 id="privacy-hosting-heading">Hosting and changes</h2>
      <p>
        The site and its database are hosted on Railway. If this policy changes, the date below will
        change with it.
      </p>
      <p class="lbm-privacy-updated">Last updated November 17, 2026.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layouts.app>
